{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"Sandboxie.Plus","latestVersion":"1.18.8","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.cf74e8cd.png","priority":1,"sha256":"cf74e8cd69e23ac5130c4a987ad778aa921bc90fe525ad12ca74d6f23b781834","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"https://xanasoft.com","copyrightUrl":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/master/LICENSE.Plus","description":"Sandboxie is a sandbox-based isolation software for 32- and 64-bit Windows NT-based operating systems.","license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.Classic","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"https://xanasoft.com","copyrightUrl":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/master/LICENSE.Plus","description":"Sandboxie is a sandbox-based isolation software for 32- and 64-bit Windows NT-based operating systems.","license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.Classic","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Sandboxie is a sandbox-based isolation software for 32- and 64-bit Windows NT-based operating systems.\nIt is developed by David Xanatos since it became open source, before that it was developed by Sophos (which acquired it from Invincea, which acquired it earlier from the original author Ronen Tzur).\nIt creates a sandbox-like isolated operating environment in which applications can be run or installed without permanently modifying the local or mapped drive.\nSuch an isolated virtual environment allows controlled testing of untrusted programs and web surfing.","moniker":"sandboxie-plus","name":"Sandboxie-Plus","packageUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie","publisher":"http://xanasoft.com/","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/issues","publisherUrl":"https://xanasoft.com/","releaseNotes":"0 5 5\nRelease Notes\nSandboxie Plus 1.18.8 / Classic 5.73.8 brings important compatibility improvements for Firefox and other sandboxed browsers, with a particular focus on fixing video playback issues.\nVideo playback now works correctly in sandboxed Firefox on websites such as ESPN that rely on mediaCapabilities.decodingInfo() to check media support before starting playback. This resolves an issue that could leave videos unable to start on affected sites.\nThe release also improves AppContainer handling used by browsers and other applications to isolate their child processes. Fixes address missing sandbox permissions and overly restrictive substitute tokens that could prevent these processes from starting or accessing required system resources. Microsoft Edge can again use the corrected substitute token without enabling UnRestrictAppContainerToken by default.\nA security fix addresses an out-of-bounds read in the GUI proxy’s MapWindowPoints handler that could expose service heap data to sandboxed callers. The Import Boxes workflow has also been corrected, allowing users to choose where imported sandboxes are created.\nFor existing sandboxes, the new fixboxdacls command in KmdUtil.exe adds missing AppContainer access permissions. Advanced configuration options provide additional control: KeepBroadGroupsInAppContainerToken=n restores the previous all-deny-only substitute token behavior, NeutralizeLowBoxToken=n allows direct NtCreateLowBoxToken calls through, and FakeAppContainerToken=n now allows sandboxed programs to create real AppContainer child processes.\nFor a full list of changes please review the change log.\nYou can support the project through donations, any help will be greatly appreciated.\nIf you have issues with an update installation, just uninstall the previous version keeping the sandboxie.ini and reinstall the new build.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/releases/tag/v1.18.8","tags":["sandbox"]}},"longDescription":"Sandboxie is a sandbox-based isolation software for 32- and 64-bit Windows NT-based operating systems.\nIt is developed by David Xanatos since it became open source, before that it was developed by Sophos (which acquired it from Invincea, which acquired it earlier from the original author Ronen Tzur).\nIt creates a sandbox-like isolated operating environment in which applications can be run or installed without permanently modifying the local or mapped drive.\nSuch an isolated virtual environment allows controlled testing of untrusted programs and web surfing.","moniker":"sandboxie-plus","name":"Sandboxie-Plus","packageUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie","publisher":"http://xanasoft.com/","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/issues","publisherUrl":"https://xanasoft.com/","releaseNotes":"0 5 5\nRelease Notes\nSandboxie Plus 1.18.8 / Classic 5.73.8 brings important compatibility improvements for Firefox and other sandboxed browsers, with a particular focus on fixing video playback issues.\nVideo playback now works correctly in sandboxed Firefox on websites such as ESPN that rely on mediaCapabilities.decodingInfo() to check media support before starting playback. This resolves an issue that could leave videos unable to start on affected sites.\nThe release also improves AppContainer handling used by browsers and other applications to isolate their child processes. Fixes address missing sandbox permissions and overly restrictive substitute tokens that could prevent these processes from starting or accessing required system resources. Microsoft Edge can again use the corrected substitute token without enabling UnRestrictAppContainerToken by default.\nA security fix addresses an out-of-bounds read in the GUI proxy’s MapWindowPoints handler that could expose service heap data to sandboxed callers. The Import Boxes workflow has also been corrected, allowing users to choose where imported sandboxes are created.\nFor existing sandboxes, the new fixboxdacls command in KmdUtil.exe adds missing AppContainer access permissions. Advanced configuration options provide additional control: KeepBroadGroupsInAppContainerToken=n restores the previous all-deny-only substitute token behavior, NeutralizeLowBoxToken=n allows direct NtCreateLowBoxToken calls through, and FakeAppContainerToken=n now allows sandboxed programs to create real AppContainer child processes.\nFor a full list of changes please review the change log.\nYou can support the project through donations, any help will be greatly appreciated.\nIf you have issues with an update installation, just uninstall the previous version keeping the sandboxie.ini and reinstall the new build.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/sandboxie-plus/Sandboxie/releases/tag/v1.18.8","tags":["sandbox"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.18.8/app.json","detailSha256":"b9108ee6e287a0da9381cf5016bbd6f783936420d03872b8b5b84f118302e808","releaseDate":"2026-11-10","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.18.8"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.18.7/app.json","detailSha256":"396499a106805f88563504dca79f0a9c30d11021b5a1d9bd5493cf98103fd763","releaseDate":"2026-11-10","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.18.7"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.18.6/app.json","detailSha256":"afc76d5e5e508741e2d2c4250f692aed2ad4d0499b125a8cdc85f689c6fb11a1","releaseDate":"2026-10-11","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.18.6"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.18.5/app.json","detailSha256":"c30cfc9931becf8090357a7de3aba6c34c86070f8f798c69a6f5ff6ee0a09f07","releaseDate":"2026-09-25","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.18.5"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.18.4/app.json","detailSha256":"04308965026a62c7dd380d25b595029f631cdff182944cbfe614f46b5d075305","releaseDate":"2026-09-06","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.18.4"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPa